Steps:
1. Send a POST request to /api/auth/signin with the payload in testData.
2. Verify the response status and body format.

Test Data: {
  "username": "testuser",
  "password": "password123"
}

Expected Result:
HTTP 200 OK response with a JSON body containing: {
  "status": "success",
  "message": "User signed in successfully",
  "data": {
    "id": <non-null number>,
    "username": "testuser",
    "email": "testuser@example.com",
    "roles": ["ROLE_USER"]
  },
  "meta": null
}
The 'Authorization' header contains a valid JWT token starting with 'Bearer '.

HTTP 200 OK response with a JSON body containing: {
  "status": "success",
  "message": "Orders retrieved successfully",
  "data": {
    "content": [<list of items>],
    "totalElements": <total number of items>,
    "totalPages": <total pages>,
    "pageable": {
      "pageNumber": 0,
      "pageSize": 10
    }
  },
  "meta": {
    "total": <total number of items>,
    "page": 0,
    "pages": <total pages>
  }
}

HTTP 200 OK response with a JSON body containing: {
  "status": "success",
  "message": "Orders retrieved successfully",
  "data": {
    "content": [<list of 5 items>],
    "totalElements": <total number of items>,
    "totalPages": <total pages>,
    "pageable": {
      "pageNumber": 1,
      "pageSize": 5
    }
  },
  "meta": {
    "total": <total number of items>,
    "page": 1,
    "pages": <total pages>
  }
}

